---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const b='/equipment/08-09/',manual='https://www.artisantg.com/info/pfeiffer_vacuum_balzers_hlt_160_manual_2021322125736.pdf#page=2',outline='https://nfc.arizona.edu/sites/default/files/2022-02/balzers-_short_operating_instructions.tif__0.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Balzers HLT 160 leak detector" description="Compare sealed inert fixtures with a simulated detector, blank correction and a declared acceptance threshold." wide={true}><article class="equipment" id="hlt160"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/08-09/">← Equipment 08-09</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#hlt-evidence">Reference sheet</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">08-09 / SEALED PACKAGE METROLOGY</p><h2>Two leak standards, one threshold</h2><p class="eq-lede">Capture a synthetic blank, then replay the low and high fixtures. Their known leak rates bracket the declared limit. A third fixture tests the gray area where uncertainty crosses the limit.</p></header>
<div class="h-cols"><section><h3>Balzers HLT 160</h3><canvas id="hlt-model" aria-label="Orbitable Balzers HLT 160 with top port and front controls"></canvas><p id="hlt-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="hlt-front">Whole unit / reset view</button><button id="hlt-port">Test port</button><button id="hlt-control">Controller close-up</button><button id="hlt-rear">Rear view</button><p>Click the upper two keys in the controller view: the lower one captures a blank, the higher one replays the trace. Click the port or model capsule to toggle the virtual fixture.</p></section>
<section><h3>Virtual bench</h3><p id="hlt-state"></p><label>Sealed inert fixture<select id="hlt-fixture"><option value="low">Low: 4.0 × 10⁻¹⁰ Pa·m³/s</option><option value="high">High: 1.6 × 10⁻⁹ Pa·m³/s</option><option value="near">Near limit: 9.8 × 10⁻¹⁰ Pa·m³/s</option></select></label><label>Replay window, seconds<input type="number" id="hlt-duration" min="3" max="20" step="any" value="16"/></label><label>Teaching threshold, Pa·m³/s<input type="number" id="hlt-limit" min="1e-10" max="5e-9" step="any" value="1e-9"/></label><div><button id="hlt-mount">Remove virtual fixture</button><button id="hlt-blank">Capture blank</button><button id="hlt-run">Replay trace</button><button id="hlt-reset">Restore example</button></div><p id="hlt-status" role="status"></p></section></div>
<section><h3>Blank-corrected signal</h3><canvas id="hlt-plot" width="960" height="344" aria-label="Blank-corrected leak trace, threshold and averaged tail"></canvas><p id="hlt-read" role="status"></p><p>The dashed line marks the selected threshold. The green region marks the last 16 samples. An unsettled trace is not assigned a rate; an uncertainty interval crossing the limit gets no pass or fail.</p><button id="hlt-json">Download replay JSON</button><button id="hlt-csv">Download trace CSV</button><p><a href={b+'example-low.json'}>Low example</a> · <a href={b+'example-high.json'}>High example</a>. The JSON includes the blank, counts, gain, raw and corrected curves, package ID and revision, criterion and result.</p></section>
<section id="hlt-evidence"><h3>Configuration and evidence</h3><p>Balzers HLT 160 as shown in the <a href={manual}>manufacturer’s guide BG 800 387 BE/B (9401), printed p. 1</a> and <a href={outline}>Balzers addendum BG 800 430 BE/A (9609), cover outline</a>. This is a nominal-scale original reconstruction, not dimensional factory data. Main shell is modeled as roughly 520 × 498 × 260 mm, with protrusions and a removable virtual fixture outside that envelope. Rear details are illustrative and controller mappings are simulator-only.</p>
<div class="h-cols"><figure><img src={b+'station.webp'} alt="Original model of Balzers HLT 160 cabinet and control column"/><figcaption>Original three-quarter overview matching the photographed cabinet, side cylinder, top port and offset controller.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={b+'port.webp'} alt="Original model of top test port holding the virtual capsule"/><figcaption>Original port close-up. The blue capsule and its dimensions are site-designed teaching geometry.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>A synthetic step approaches the fixture’s assigned flow with a 1.25 s time constant. Subtract a separately acquired blank average, divide by the declared normalized gain, and average the tail if its halves agree within 5 × 10⁻¹² Pa·m³/s over one second. The threshold decision uses the declared fixture uncertainty, not a general instrument confidence interval. For units, 1 mbar·L/s = 0.1 Pa·m³/s. The examples are simulated, not archival readings. The controls do not model real gas or vacuum handling, actual detector response, or operational procedures.</p>
<div class="h-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual, Pa·m³/s</th><th>Decision</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Low</td><td>(4.0 ± 0.2) × 10⁻¹⁰</td><td>3.99997 × 10⁻¹⁰</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>High</td><td>(1.60 ± 0.05) × 10⁻⁹</td><td>1.59999 × 10⁻⁹</td><td>Fail</td></tr><tr><td>Near</td><td>Uncertainty spans 10⁻⁹</td><td>9.79994 × 10⁻¹⁰</td><td>Indeterminate</td></tr><tr><td>High, 3 s replay</td><td>Not settled</td><td>No estimate</td><td>Unstable</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={b+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={b+'hlt160.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={b+'leak-replay.mjs'}>Replay and state functions</a> · <a href={b+'vr.json'}>VR ray bounds and asset budget</a>. No headset test or physical calibration claim.</p></section></article></Layout>
